Body is **4496 against a 4500 ceiling** — I paid for ~470 words of new material in full, but there is now zero headroom. Every cut came from duplication, not evidence: the doubled Type 3 case, the Ballerina Farm paragraph, the tradwife empathy-turn recap (redundant now that the scratch section carries the origin), and overlong quotes. An editor pass should cut a section before adding a sentence — the "Why the label stuck in the first place" H3 is now the most compressible thing left, since the lupus material took over the origin argument it used to share.
